From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:39:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build a position-independent multilib for SPU target libraries.

-fpic links (SPURS jobs, policy modules) select pic/ copies of libgcc, newlib,
libsupc++ and libstdc++. Fixed-address images
are unaffected by which copy they get. The pic build keeps its absolute data words
(pointer tables) for the image's fixup table, so it may not refuse run-time
relocations. The __ea (mea64) variant stays unbuilt as before.

(Ported to GCC 16 from patches/spu/gcc-9.5.0/0010-spu-pic-multilib.patch.)
---
 gcc/config/spu/t-spu-elf | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/t-spu-elf b/gcc/config/spu/t-spu-elf
index 7f2363133a2..0dbe980a71b 100644
--- a/gcc/config/spu/t-spu-elf
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/t-spu-elf
@@ -15,7 +15,10 @@
 #  <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
 
 # Multi-lib support.
-MULTILIB_OPTIONS=mea64
+MULTILIB_OPTIONS=fpic
+MULTILIB_DIRNAMES=pic
+MULTILIB_MATCHES=fpic=fPIC
+MULTILIB_EXTRA_OPTS=mno-error-reloc
 
 spu.o: $(CONFIG_H) $(SYSTEM_H) coretypes.h $(TM_H) \
   $(RTL_H) $(REGS_H) hard-reg-set.h dumpfile.h \
